1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,448
The defender moved.

2
00:00:01,448 --> 00:00:02,200
Or did he?

3
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:06,075
Before the Roar.

4
00:00:06,075 --> 00:00:11,450
Five specialists investigate the play, then show you what the evidence can actually support.

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,628
The winger moves wide.

6
00:00:13,628 --> 00:00:16,449
The defender shifts toward the same side.

7
00:00:16,449 --> 00:00:18,800
There may be space opening inside.

8
00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:22,009
An off-ball run means moving without the ball.

9
00:00:22,009 --> 00:00:25,800
Watch whether the defender follows, or holds their position.

10
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:29,844
Two completed passes move the ball twenty-three point seven metres forward.

11
00:00:29,844 --> 00:00:32,800
That calculation does not explain the defender's intention.

12
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:36,160
Coinciding movements don't prove causation.

13
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:39,800
Change the observation, and this claim must change.

14
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:41,705
The passes stand.

15
00:00:41,705 --> 00:00:45,363
The interpretation remains conditional.

16
00:00:45,363 --> 00:00:47,650
Let's test the evidence.

17
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:50,981
Here is the actual correction, without a cut.

18
00:00:50,981 --> 00:00:52,932
Apply the revised observation.

19
00:00:52,932 --> 00:00:54,819
Thirteen metres becomes zero.

20
00:00:54,819 --> 00:00:56,895
The movement claim is withdrawn.

21
00:00:56,895 --> 00:00:58,405
The two passes survive.

22
00:00:58,405 --> 00:01:03,250
This demonstration runs deterministic checks; it makes no new model request.

23
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:06,470
The corrected revision reaches Pocket Director.

24
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:09,085
The same evidence, explained for a different viewer.

25
00:01:09,085 --> 00:01:11,800
Football knowledge should never be the price of entry.

26
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:15,159
Measure the fictional sample, or upload compatible footage.

27
00:01:15,159 --> 00:01:19,800
These measurements come from controlled synthetic video, separate from the cinematic film.

28
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:25,824
Inspect the receipts: model requests, calculations, restored stages, and failures.

29
00:01:25,824 --> 00:01:28,800
More voices don't prove better commentary.

30
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:31,458
Container Apps receives the event.

31
00:01:31,458 --> 00:01:32,951
Entra secures access.

32
00:01:32,951 --> 00:01:35,191
Azure OpenAI powers specialists.

33
00:01:35,191 --> 00:01:36,345
Foundry advises.

34
00:01:36,345 --> 00:01:38,789
Blob Storage preserves checkpoints.

35
00:01:38,789 --> 00:01:41,300
The evidence gate controls delivery.

36
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:47,346
Watch the play.

37
00:01:47,346 --> 00:01:48,941
Question the story.

38
00:01:48,941 --> 00:01:50,296
Before the Roar.

39
00:01:50,296 --> 00:01:52,050
Every play has a why.
